       <\/ul>\n\n                            <div class=\"mt-3\">\n                                                                    <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                       target=\"_blank\"\n                                       class=\"btn view-btn btn-sm\">\n                                        View Brochure\n                                    <\/a>\n                                \n                                <a target=\"_blank\"\n                                   href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>SEO Keyword Research Tools<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Let\u2019s dive deep into the best keyword research tools for SEO in 2026:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Google Keyword Planner<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"696\" height=\"230\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-keyword-planner.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-7316\" style=\"width:345px;height:114px\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-keyword-planner.webp 696w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-keyword-planner-300x99.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-keyword-planner-150x50.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Google is the dominant search engine. So, it\u2019s no surprise that it offers the best free keyword research tool known as <a href=\"https:\/\/ads.google.com\/intl\/en_in\/home\/tools\/keyword-planner\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Google Keyword Planner<\/a>. It is a great place to start your keyword search, especially when you use Google Ads for your paid ad campaigns.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you want to use this tool, you need to set up an AdWords account, but you don&#8217;t have to create an ad. If you use it for your ad campaigns, it allows you to select competitive bids and budgets.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It\u2019s easy to use and navigate, so it\u2019s an excellent option for beginners. You simply need to input a keyword, multiple keywords, or a website link, and Keyword Planner will provide you with a list of relevant keywords and simple metrics so that you can determine the level of competition for each keyword and total searches (global and local) for each one. It also gives data regarding monthly searches, bidding information, and related keywords.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Users can also get insights into historical statistics and details regarding keyword performance. If you want, you can get a new list of keywords generated by multiplying different lists of keywords.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>However, with the transition of Google Keyword Tool to Keyword Planner, the tool removed various functionalities. So, it might lack a few features and functionalities that you can find in other tools, but it makes up for it by offering you data directly from Google. Anyone with a Google Ads account can use this tool for free.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. SEMrush<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/semrush-1024x576.webp\" alt=\"SEMrush\" class=\"wp-image-7317\" style=\"width:310px;height:174px\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/semrush-1024x576.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/semrush-300x169.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/semrush-768x432.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/semrush-150x84.webp 150w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/semrush.webp 1366w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.semrush.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">SEMrush<\/a> is a well-known keyword research tool that helps advertisers simplify and manage their SEO tasks. It is a competitive research tool that offers a range of keywords for different marketing strategies, such as <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-ppc\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">PPC<\/a>, content, competitor research, social media, and more.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>One reason that it is considered among the top SEO keyword research tools is it lets users identify competitors\u2019 keywords to explore better marketing opportunities to attain higher search engine rankings on Google, Bing, and Yahoo.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Use this tool to compare various domains and evaluate the competitive landscape, such as common keywords, their positions in organic and paid results, and their history of rises and drops. It is user-friendly, giving you a sneak peek into trending topics and keyword popularity. You can find what attracts the audience to accelerate your business growth. Its visually appealing charts make it easier for users to understand trends and analyze results.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Google Trends<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"866\" height=\"650\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-trends.webp\" alt=\"google trends\" class=\"wp-image-7206\" style=\"width:221px;height:166px\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-trends.webp 866w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-trends-300x225.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-trends-768x576.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/google-trends-150x113.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 866px) 100vw, 866px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/trends.google.com\/trends\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Google Trends<\/a> is another fantastic tool that helps you find the popularity of different keywords and their search volumes over time and across multiple locations. You can filter keywords based on search history, location, and category.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You just have to input details, and it will provide you with detailed results, showing the web interest around a specific search term, reasons for the interest, source of traffic, and similar keywords. Apart from giving static keyword volume numbers, it also generates interactive and easy-to-understand graphs that you can download and embed on your website.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can get more in-depth information about keywords to know their relative popularity over time. While preparing data, it doesn\u2019t include repeated queries from a single user over a short span, enhancing the result and making it more accurate.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This is one of the most reliable tools for grouping searches that it assumes to be the same. If you are not able to pick between two keyword variations for your next blog post, then Google Trends is one of the top keyword research SEO tools to 